Fork PR (same branch, for browsing): https://github.com/AlexPerrin/OpenRune-Server/pull/5

## Summary

Opening the fullscreen world map overwrites `resizable_stone_arrangement` with the map frame's flag. Closing back to a resizable frame sets it again, but closing to a fixed frame doesn't, and logging out with the map open saves the map's value. The player's classic/modern stone choice is lost, and the next login whose saved frame doesn't match the client mode falls back on the wrong flag.

This PR first also kept the fullscreen map frame out of the login gameframe and the fallbacks. #315 (Ides of Milk) has since done that on `main` with `Gameframe.isGameplay`, so that part is gone: `main` is merged in (a merge commit, no rebase) and the branch uses `isGameplay` throughout. What remains is the stone-arrangement restore:
- Moving from a gameplay frame to the fullscreen map remembers `resizable_stone_arrangement`; moving back puts it back, also when closing to a fixed frame and at logout while the map is open. While the map is open the flag still changes as before.
- The remembered value is a server-side varbit, as asked in review: `varbit.gameframe_stone_before_fullscreen` (0 nothing saved, 1 classic, 2 modern) on a new `varp.gameframe_state` (scope Temp, transmit Never: not saved, never sent), in the gameframe pack's `gameframe_vars.toml`. Ids 65471 / 65447 from `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py`; `--check` is clean on the merged branch.

